        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d5e9c9df-a980-5d17-ae7e-f1ad886ba676",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Madison Avenue, East 23rd Street, Madison Square Park, Central Park\n- Buildings: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, Met Life Tower, 432 Park Avenue, Princess Tower\n- Companies: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company, Credit Suisse, Hedden Construction Company\n\nFacts:\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, also called the Met Life Tower, is a landmark skyscraper in Manhattan, New York City, on Madison Avenue near East 23rd Street and across from Madison Square Park.\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower is also identified as being located at One Madison Avenue in New York, New York.\n- The clock tower portion of the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower contains a hotel at 5 Madison Avenue.\n- The office building occupying the rest of the block is referred to as 1 Madison Avenue and is occupied primarily by Credit Suisse.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\n- Princess Tower was the tallest residential building in the world from 2012 until 2015.\n- In 2015, 432 Park Avenue in New York City overtook Princess Tower as the tallest residential building in the world.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
